Fri Aug 21 08:56:25 UTC 2026 - Martin Pluskal <mpluskal@suse.com>

- Update to 0.27.0 (matches Factory python-torch 2.12.0):
  * Add lanczos interpolation for v2.Resize on CPU (AVX2/NEON)
  * Add KeyPoints and rotated bounding-box support in v2
    transforms
  * Add GIF and WEBP image decoders; decode_image() accepts paths
  * Resize can target the longest edge via max_size
  * Remove the video_reader backend (use TorchCodec / pyav)
  * Vectorize masks_to_boxes; add rotated-box IoU
  * Fix v2.ElasticTransform normalization and bbox clamping
- Add fix-gif-decoder-oob.patch (pytorch/vision#9520, from 0.28):
  * GIF decoder heap OOB read/write on crafted images
    (GHSA-vp9x-48wq-4wc3; no CVE assigned)
- Build CPU-only against Factory torch (FORCE_CUDA=0, no NVJPEG)
- Drop ffmpeg BuildRequires: video_reader was removed upstream
- Switch the build to %pyproject_wheel / %pyproject_install
- Run %check outside the source tree so the compiled _C extension
  is imported
- Declare runtime Requires for numpy, Pillow and torch (the
  generator does not pick them up from this setuptools wheel)
- Strip unused shebangs from imported .py modules

-------------------------------------------------------------------
Fri Aug 21 08:47:56 UTC 2026 - Martin Pluskal <mpluskal@suse.com>

- Build against distro ffmpeg via pkgconfig(libavcodec) and friends instead of the retired ffmpeg-6 packages.

